# 必考词 Unit24
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2023红宝书考研英语词汇-必考词
# 描述: 必考词Unit24核心高频词汇

{{wage}}{/weɪdʒ/}}{n. 工资；v. 发动}}{{The workers demanded higher wages and better conditions.}}

{{wander}}{/ˈwɒndər/}}{v. 漫步；偏离}}{{He wandered through the old town, enjoying the scenery.}}

{{warn}}{/wɔːrn/}}{v. 警告；提醒}}{{The doctor warned him about the dangers of smoking.}}

{{waste}}{/weɪst/}}{v. 浪费；n. 废物}}{{Do not waste your time on unimportant matters.}}

{{wealth}}{/welθ/}}{n. 财富；丰富}}{{The region is known for its natural wealth and resources.}}

{{welfare}}{/ˈwelfeər/}}{n. 福利；幸福}}{{The government should invest more in public welfare programs.}}

{{whereas}}{/weərˈæz/}}{conj. 然而；鉴于}}{{He likes classical music, whereas his brother prefers rock.}}

{{widespread}}{/ˈwaɪdspred/}}{adj. 广泛的；普遍的}}{{There is widespread concern about the effects of pollution.}}

{{withdraw}}{/wɪðˈdrɔː/}}{v. 撤回；退出}}{{The company decided to withdraw from the market.}}

{{witness}}{/ˈwɪtnəs/}}{n. 目击者；v. 目击}}{{Several witnesses testified at the trial.}}

{{worthwhile}}{/ˌwɜːrθˈwaɪl/}}{adj. 值得做的}}{{Volunteering is a worthwhile experience for young people.}}

{{yield}}{/jiːld/}}{v. 产出；屈服；n. 产量}}{{The farm yields a large crop of wheat every year.}}

{{zone}}{/zəʊn/}}{n. 地区；区域}}{{The area has been designated as a special economic zone.}}

{{abundant}}{/əˈbʌndənt/}}{adj. 丰富的；充裕的}}{{The region has abundant natural resources.}}

{{academy}}{/əˈkædəmi/}}{n. 学院；研究院}}{{She was admitted to the Royal Academy of Music.}}

{{accord}}{/əˈkɔːrd/}}{n. 一致；协议；v. 相符合}}{{The two nations signed a peace accord.}}

{{accumulate}}{/əˈkjuːmjəleɪt/}}{v. 积累；堆积}}{{Over time, dust accumulates on surfaces.}}

{{accurate}}{/ˈækjərət/}}{{adj. 准确的；精确的}}{{The weather forecast is usually quite accurate.}}

{{accustom}}{/əˈkʌstəm/}}{v. 使习惯}}{{It took time to accustom herself to the new environment.}}

{{acute}}{/əˈkjuːt/}}{adj. 急性的；敏锐的}}{{The hospital has a ward for acute patients.}}

{{adequate}}{/ˈædɪkwət/}}{adj. 足够的；适当的}}{{The funding is not adequate for the project's needs.}}

{{adhere}}{/ədˈhɪər/}}{v. 粘附；坚持}}{{All employees must adhere to the company's code of conduct.}}

{{adjacent}}{/əˈdʒeɪsnt/}}{adj. 邻近的；毗连的}}{{The park is adjacent to the school campus.}}

{{administer}}{/ədˈmɪnɪstər/}}{v. 管理；执行}}{{The nurse administered the vaccine to the patient.}}

{{adverse}}{/ˈædvɜːrs/}}{adj. 不利的；有害的}}{{Adverse weather conditions delayed the flight.}}

{{advocate}}{/ˈædvəkeɪt/}}{v. 提倡；n. 倡导者}}{{She advocates for equal rights for all citizens.}}

{{affirm}}{/əˈfɜːrm/}}{v. 肯定；确认}}{{The court affirmed the decision of the lower court.}}

{{agenda}}{/əˈdʒendə/}}{n. 议程；日程安排}}{{The agenda for the meeting was sent out in advance.}}

{{agitate}}{/ˈædʒɪteɪt/}}{v. 搅动；使不安}}{{The news agitated the public and sparked protests.}}

{{alert}}{/əˈlɜːrt/}}{adj. 警觉的；v. 使警觉}}{{The system alerts users when unusual activity is detected.}}

{{alien}}{/ˈeɪliən/}}{adj. 外国的；n. 外星人}}{{The concept was completely alien to his way of thinking.}}

{{allege}}{/əˈledʒ/}}{v. 宣称；指控}}{{The newspaper alleged that the official had accepted bribes.}}

{{alleviate}}{/əˈliːvieɪt/}}{v. 减轻；缓解}}{{The new policy aims to alleviate poverty in rural areas.}}

{{allocate}}{/ˈæləkeɪt/}}{v. 分配；拨出}}{{Resources were allocated equally among the departments.}}

{{ambiguity}}{/ˌæmbɪˈɡjuːəti/}}{n. 歧义；含糊不清}}{{The ambiguity of the contract led to a legal dispute.}}

{{amend}}{/əˈmend/}}{v. 修正；改进}}{{The law was amended to include new provisions.}}

{{analogy}}{/əˈnælədʒi/}}{n. 类比；类推}}{{He drew an analogy between the brain and a computer.}}

{{anticipate}}{/ænˈtɪsɪpeɪt/}}{v. 预期；期望}}{{We did not anticipate such a strong response from the public.}}

{{apparatus}}{/ˌæpəˈreɪtəs/}}{n. 器械；机构}}{{The laboratory is equipped with modern scientific apparatus.}}

{{appreciable}}{/əˈpriːʃəbl/}}{adj. 可观的；明显的}}{{There has been an appreciable improvement in air quality.}}
